%description:

Tcp.windowShrinkAllowed:yes-first -- the first offer is half the buffer.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the offered window follows the free receive buffer and may move its right
edge back, as Linux with tcp_shrink_window=1 ...; the first offer is half the buffer. RFC 9293
says that a receiver SHOULD NOT shrink the window (SHLD-14)".

The classes: no (false, the default) and yes (true), with the facets first and shrink. The
code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() makes the first offer half the buffer with
true; TcpConnection::selectRcvWnd() offers the free buffer, charged at the truesize of the
segments, and TcpConnection::updateRcvWnd() lets the right edge move back; with false, the
right edge never moves back. This test separates "yes" from "no", whose first offer is the whole buffer.

Host under test: host2, with a receive buffer of 32768 bytes (precondition: the class needs a
buffer), whose application does not read; host1 sends 100000 bytes. Observation: level 1, the SYN-ACK of host2 offers 16384 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowShrinkAllowed
%# class: yes-first
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowShrinkAllowed
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowShrinkAllowedYesFirst")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.window == 16384")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowShrinkAllowedYesFirst compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowShrinkAllowed = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 32768B
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowShrinkAllowedYesFirst: PASS
